<h2 id="aprendizaje">What I learned <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i> </h2>
<p> 
  • Images — Configuration and dependencies needed for an application to run.<br /> 
  • Containers — Running instances of an image. <br /> 
  • Ports — Exposure of the container to the host. <br /> 
  • Networks — Virtual connections that allow communication between containers. <br /> 
  • Volumes — Persistent storage spaces to keep data beyond the container's lifecycle. <br /> 
  • Docker Compose — Tool for defining and running multi-container applications through YAML files. <br /> 
  • Docker Compose Dev — Special configuration for development environments. <br /> 
  • Hot Reload — Technique that reflects code changes automatically inside the container without rebuilding the image. <br /> 
</p>